From fc5ba6381f2bbcb64ea2f9dcabf2174ec546b5e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:42:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: dt-bindings: qcom: Describe PM8226 L3 active-only
 voter

CPR can require a higher MX floor while Pronto retains its fixed L3
consumer request. Describe the optional l3-ao voter separately from l3
so their consumer constraint ranges need not intersect. Both nodes vote
on one physical LDO using maximum active voltage and enable requests;
only the normal voter supplies the sleep policy.

Require the normal l3 node with l3-ao, restrict the alias to PM8226 and
reject suspend settings on the active-only node. Existing trees without
the alias retain their current meaning.

This is an opt-in feature prerequisite, not a fix to an existing upstream
CPR board. Codex generated the change and its host qualification. Human
review and DCO certification remain pending. Nothing has been submitted.

Backport this prerequisite to maintained Linux 6.18.63. The complete
seventeen-change batch passes native ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT object
builds with the MSM8926 feature enabled and disabled. CPU-idle is ARM
only. Host fault models use synthetic services and normal LeakSanitizer;
firmware, electrical and physical suspend acceptance remain open.

Codex prepared this local backport and verification. Original authors,
dates, licenses and human attribution tags are retained. Human DCO and
review remain pending. No phone access or publication occurred.

Backported from commit ec99962a30bb ("regulator: dt-bindings: qcom:
Describe PM8226 L3 active-only voter")
---
 .../regulator/qcom,smd-rpm-regulator.yaml     | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,smd-rpm-regulator.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,smd-rpm-regulator.yaml
index b7241ce975b96..8c68c3cdbe35e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,smd-rpm-regulator.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/qcom,smd-rpm-regulator.yaml
@@ -39,6 +39,13 @@ description:
   l11, l12, l13, l14, l15, l16, l17, l18, l19, l20, l21, l22, l23, l24, l25,
   l26, l27, l28, lvs1
 
+  PM8226 also supports l3-ao as an active-only voter for the same physical
+  regulator as l3. When present, l3 and l3-ao have independent consumer
+  constraints. Their enable and voltage requests are combined using a maximum
+  for the active set. Only l3 contributes to the sleep set; explicit suspend
+  settings on l3 override its normal sleep vote. These nodes describe two
+  voters, not two independent physical supplies.
+
   For pm8841, s1, s2, s3, s4, s5, s6, s7, s8
 
   For pm8909, s1, s2, l1, l2, l3, l4, l5, l6, l7, l8, l9, l10, l11, l12, l13,
@@ -107,6 +114,15 @@ properties:
       - qcom,rpm-pmr735a-regulators
       - qcom,rpm-pms405-regulators
 
+  l3-ao:
+    $ref: regulator.yaml#
+    description: PM8226 L3 active-only voter, paired with l3
+    properties:
+      regulator-state-mem: false
+      regulator-state-disk: false
+      regulator-state-standby: false
+    unevaluatedProperties: false
+
 patternProperties:
   ".*-supply$":
     description: Input supply phandle(s) for this node
@@ -118,6 +134,18 @@ patternProperties:
 
 additionalProperties: false
 
+allOf:
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          const: qcom,rpm-pm8226-regulators
+    then:
+      dependentRequired:
+        l3-ao: [l3]
+    else:
+      properties:
+        l3-ao: false
+
 required:
   - compatible
 
-- 
